{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["And if the household be too little — that they cannot eat it all." "According to the number — a count, as written: ״ויהי המכס לה׳ מן הצאן״. The mem is root, like the mem of 'molekh.' 'Mikhseh' is like: ״שכבת הטל״. But 'tikhussu' is derived from the root k-s-s, like 'tisovvu' or 'savav.' It is not derived from 'mikhes' at all. And even if the mem of 'mikhseh' were an addition and not from the root of the word — like 'mitsvah,' 'mikneh,' 'mar'eh,' 'ma'aseh' — 'tikhussu' would still not be from 'mikhes' but from the root כסה עשה ראה. [The following passage is textually difficult:] מחסופי למ\"ד פעל של ה' שכולם אות שאחרי המ\"ם בחטף — תקוה תגרת ידיך מצות, אבל מן שב, קם, ויגר מואב — יאמר תשובה תקומה, ומגורתם אביא להם — חטף באות ראשונה."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {1 "The latter half of this comment is textually obscure and possibly corrupt; it is rendered hyper-literally. The argument appears to be a technical lexicographical comparison of prefixed-mem forms and vowel patterns (ḥaṭef vowels) to distinguish root vs. prefixed mem in various Hebrew words, but the received text is garbled."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:11.856041799Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}